G<sup>+</sup> lack\nArcS homologues. Using comparative genomics approaches, two families\nthat could functionally replace ArcS in these organisms were identified:\n(1) GAT-QueC, a two-domain family with an N-terminal glutamine amidotransferase\nclass-II domain fused to a domain homologous to QueC, the enzyme that\nproduces preQ<sub>0</sub> and (2) QueF-like, a family homologous to\nthe bacterial enzyme catalyzing the reduction of preQ<sub>0</sub> to\n7-aminomethyl-7-deazaguanine. Here we show that these two protein\nfamilies are able to catalyze the formation of G<sup>+</sup> in a\nheterologous system. Structure and sequence comparisons of crenarchaeal\nand euryarchaeal arcTGTs suggest the crenarchaeal enzymes have broader\nsubstrate specificity. These results led to a new model for the synthesis\nand salvage of G<sup>+</sup> in Crenarchaeota.", "funding": null, "funding_list": [], "version": 1, "status": "public", "size": 2343571, "created_date": "2016-02-22T05:36:35Z", "modified_date": "2023-06-18T05:39:01Z", "is_public": true, "is_confidential": false, "is_metadata_record": false, "confidential_reason": "", "metadata_reason": "", "license": {"value": 10, "name": "CC BY-NC 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/"}, "tags": ["preQ 0", "enzyme", "Crenarchaeota", "tRNA", "crenarchaeal", "lack ArcS homologues", "arcTGT"], "keywords": ["preQ 0", "enzyme", "Crenarchaeota", "tRNA", "crenarchaeal", "lack ArcS homologues", "arcTGT"], "categories": [{"id": 4, "title": "Biochemistry", "parent_id": 38, "path": "", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 10}, {"id": 7, "title": "Medicine", "parent_id": 48, "path": "", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 10}, {"id": 8, "title": "Microbiology", "parent_id": 48, "path": "", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 10}, {"id": 13, "title": "Genetics", "parent_id": 48, "path": "", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 10}, {"id": 24, "title": "Evolutionary Biology", "parent_id": 48, "path": "", "source_id": "", "taxonomy_id": 10}, {"id"